  "id": "cilium",
  "term": "cilium",
  "definition": "A cilium is a cellular projection that serves movement or sensing functions and depends on a distinct set of proteins to work properly. Its base forms a gate-like transition zone, where the centriole’s microtubules change into those of the axoneme and where protein entry into the cilium is regulated.",
